# .graphifyignore — what the graphify knowledge graph should NOT index.
#
# Syntax: identical to .gitignore (gitignore spec, last-match-wins, `!` negates).
# Scope:  read from this directory (the scan root) and its ancestors, and live
#         during the walk; honoured alongside .gitignore, not instead of it.
#
# Policy for this repo: index the APPLICATION (code + the technical documents
# that describe how it behaves), and exclude the build process's own paperwork.
# The process artifacts are ~245K words — 82% of the document corpus on the last
# extraction — and they describe how the app was built, not how it works.

# ── build / dependency / tooling noise ──────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
graphify-out/
.DS_Store
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ── the pipeline's process artifacts (large, and not app knowledge) ─────────
# Requirements → Plan → Validation → Review transcripts and ledgers.
docs/requirements/
docs/tasks/
docs/plan*.md
docs/architecture*.md
docs/phase-changelog.md
docs/code_review/review_log.md
docs/code_review/precheck.md
# The escalation ledgers: the older markdown one AND the live JSON one.
docs/code_review/escalations.md
docs/code_review/escalations.json
# The orchestrator's run state: transient pipeline bookkeeping, not app knowledge.
docs/orchestrator_state.json

# ── deliberately KEPT (technical knowledge about this application) ──────────
#   docs/code_review/*_investigation.md        root-cause analyses with file:line
#   docs/code_review/*_permissions.md          IBKR entitlement findings
#   docs/code_review/portfolio_held_rows.md    the leaked-fixture diagnosis
#   docs/memory.md                             accumulated technical gotchas
#   docs/ibkr-api-data-inventory.md            the IBKR API surface inventory
#   docs/thinkorswim-feature-gap-analysis.md   feature-gap analysis
#   USAGE.txt, usage.md, requirements.txt

# ── operational / generated / already-summarised documents ──────────────────
# These restate the code or record the process rather than describe behaviour the
# graph could help navigate (owner call, 2026-10-26). The usage guides and the
# changelog are generated/derived; the codebase map and memory file duplicate what
# the AST already knows; the review logs and the order-code audit are review
# transcripts of removals that no longer exist in the tree.
USAGE.txt
usage.md
docs/CHANGELOG.md
docs/codebase-map.md
docs/memory.md
docs/code_review/review_log_*.md
docs/code_review/order_code_audit.md
